WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:32.166
<b>Here, Lord Krishna explains</b>

2
00:00:32.166 --> 00:00:35.791
<b>how Arjuna can stay away from 'sin'.</b>

3
00:00:35.791 --> 00:00:36.875
<b>He says,</b>

4
00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:37.875
<b>"Arjuna,</b>

5
00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:40.166
<b>whether there is gain or loss,</b>

6
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:42.208
<b>whether you find pleasure or pain, </b>

7
00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:45.000
<b>whether you achieve victory or face defeat,</b>

8
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.208
<b>when you fight viewing these as equal,</b>

9
00:00:47.208 --> 00:00:52.208
<b>free from both their attraction and worry,</b>

10
00:00:52.208 --> 00:00:55.541
<b>you shall remain free from sin."</b>

11
00:01:00.291 --> 00:01:03.791
<b>Let's understand this through this dialogue.</b>

12
00:01:03.791 --> 00:01:05.875
<b>When Arjuna asks,</b>

13
00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:07.083
<b>"Oh Madhava,</b>

14
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:11.000
<b>I accept that not performing </b>
<b>my duty will bring me sin.</b>

15
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.291
<b>But even if I perform my duty, if I fight this war,</b>

16
00:01:14.291 --> 00:01:20.250
<b>won't the sin of killing my elders and</b>
<b>teachers rest upon my head?"</b>

17
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.583
<b>In response, Lord Krishna says,</b>

18
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:23.666
<b>"Arjuna,</b>

19
00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:28.416
<b>if you fight with true discernment, </b>
<b>you won't become a bearer of sin.</b>

20
00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:33.291
<b>Because sin isn't tied to any action, but </b>
<b>to the intention hidden behind it.</b>

21
00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:37.166
<b>If the intention isn't corrupt, </b>
<b>no sin will attach itself.</b>

22
00:01:37.166 --> 00:01:40.208
<b>While fighting, you must hold no self-interest</b>

23
00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:44.208
<b>neither in victory nor defeat, </b>
<b>neither in gain nor loss."</b>

24
00:01:44.208 --> 00:01:46.666
<b>Then Arjuna asks,</b>

25
00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:47.541
<b>"Madhava,</b>

26
00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:50.500
<b>if I'm not to think of victory or defeat,</b>

27
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.625
<b>then what motivation remains to fight at all?"</b>

28
00:01:54.625 --> 00:01:55.333
<b>Then</b>

29
00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:57.041
<b>Lord Krishna speaks, saying,</b>

30
00:01:57.041 --> 00:01:58.041
<b>"Arjuna</b>

31
00:01:58.041 --> 00:01:59.583
<b>that's precisely the point.</b>

32
00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:02.916
<b>Victory and defeat are both outcomes of war,</b>

33
00:02:02.916 --> 00:02:04.625
<b>both are possible.</b>

34
00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:06.708
<b>Victory brings joy,</b>

35
00:02:06.708 --> 00:02:09.625
<b>defeat brings extreme sorrow.</b>

36
00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:13.333
<b>But if you acknowledge your spiritual form,</b>

37
00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:18.000
<b>you'll understand that in your eternal </b>
<b>existence, one victory, one defeat</b>

38
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.166
<b>how minor these events are.</b>

39
00:02:20.166 --> 00:02:22.250
<b>What difference do they make? </b>

40
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:27.833
<b>The pain of defeat or the elation of victory, </b>
<b>these are all just plays of the senses, </b>

41
00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:30.166
<b>games of this worldly realm.</b>

42
00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:33.708
<b>This way of thinking is called Sama Bhava.</b>

43
00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:34.666
<b>Sama bhava.</b>

44
00:02:34.666 --> 00:02:38.625
<b>Meaning a state of equality, </b>
<b>a sense of sameness,</b>

45
00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:43.958
<b>where nothing is higher or lower,</b>
<b>everything is balanced.</b>

46
00:02:43.958 --> 00:02:48.916
<b>So fight while maintaining balance, </b>
<b>rising above victory and defeat.</b>

47
00:02:48.916 --> 00:02:51.666
<b>In this state, you're merely performing action,</b>

48
00:02:51.666 --> 00:02:55.333
<b>without desire for gain or fear of loss.</b>

49
00:02:55.333 --> 00:03:02.041
<b>This action, free from any expectation</b>
<b>of results, is called Nishkama Karma Yoga.</b>

50
00:03:02.041 --> 00:03:04.125
<b>No sin attaches to it."</b>

51
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.791
<b>The effort here is to</b>

52
00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:16.791
<b>help Arjuna understand that Nishkama Karma</b>

53
00:03:16.791 --> 00:03:24.875
<b>action without desire for results - is supreme.</b>

54
00:03:24.875 --> 00:03:30.958
<b>In personal life too, </b>
<b>we can understand it this way.</b>

55
00:03:30.958 --> 00:03:33.250
<b>This world is complex,</b>

56
00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:39.125
<b>multiple events combine to</b>
<b>determine any outcome.</b>

57
00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:42.500
<b>You prepared extensively for an exam,</b>

58
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.833
<b>but fell ill that day,</b>

59
00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:49.916
<b>couldn't even attend.</b>

60
00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:51.916
<b>Or your health was fine,</b>

61
00:03:51.916 --> 00:03:52.875
<b>but</b>

62
00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:57.833
<b>ink spilled on your answer sheet at the end,</b>

63
00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:00.708
<b>ruining everything written.</b>

64
00:04:00.708 --> 00:04:03.125
<b>There are countless possibilities.</b>

65
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:04.666
<b>Among these</b>

66
00:04:04.666 --> 00:04:11.291
<b>is also the possibility that </b>
<b>you might top the exam.</b>

67
00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:13.791
<b>Now think for a moment,</b>

68
00:04:13.791 --> 00:04:20.041
<b>what's under your control </b>
<b>in all these situations?</b>

69
00:04:20.041 --> 00:04:22.291
<b>What is it?</b>

70
00:04:22.291 --> 00:04:25.291
<b>Only your preparation</b>

71
00:04:25.291 --> 00:04:27.666
<b>Isn't it?</b>

72
00:04:27.666 --> 00:04:30.583
<b>If fear of poor health haunts you,</b>

73
00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:33.458
<b>it will affect your preparation.</b>

74
00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:39.291
<b>If you feel the exam is too easy,</b>

75
00:04:39.291 --> 00:04:42.458
<b>you might become lazy,</b>

76
00:04:42.458 --> 00:04:46.333
<b>and something might be missed.</b>

77
00:04:46.333 --> 00:04:55.791
<b>Isn't it futile to worry about things</b>
<b> beyond your control?</b>

78
00:04:55.791 --> 00:04:57.416
<b>Similarly,</b>

79
00:04:57.416 --> 00:05:07.625
<b>sometimes we become discouraged before</b>
<b> taking the first step towards any task,</b>

80
00:05:07.625 --> 00:05:11.125
<b>thinking something might go wrong.</b>

81
00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:14.791
<b>We never even start the work.</b>

82
00:05:14.791 --> 00:05:16.041
<b>But</b>

83
00:05:16.041 --> 00:05:19.875
<b>you know the truth</b>

84
00:05:19.875 --> 00:05:25.541
<b>you can't know all the potholes</b>
<b> in any path right at the start,</b>

85
00:05:25.541 --> 00:05:28.875
<b>you must take steps one by one,</b>

86
00:05:28.875 --> 00:05:35.250
<b>solve problems one by one.</b>

87
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:40.125
<b>Two things are absolutely clear </b>
<b>in this entire description:</b>

88
00:05:40.125 --> 00:05:44.000
<b>External circumstances are not in your control</b>

89
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.000
<b>Only</b>

90
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.291
<b>and only</b>

91
00:05:46.291 --> 00:05:51.666
<b>your actions are in your control</b>

92
00:05:51.666 --> 00:05:54.041
<b>Just perform your action,</b>

93
00:05:54.041 --> 00:05:56.583
<b>and do it with dedication.</b>

94
00:06:01.458 --> 00:06:03.208
<b>It is required of Arjuna</b>

95
00:06:03.208 --> 00:06:06.208
<b>that profit/loss,</b>

96
00:06:06.208 --> 00:06:06.875
<b>victory</b>

97
00:06:06.875 --> 00:06:08.250
<b>defeat,</b>

98
00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.125
<b>without any such expectations,</b>

99
00:06:10.125 --> 00:06:12.666
<b>he performs his duty</b>

100
00:06:12.666 --> 00:06:17.750
<b>Expectations don't help us fulfill </b>
<b>our responsibilities,</b>

101
00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:18.541
<b>but</b>

102
00:06:18.541 --> 00:06:23.791
<b>often become obstacles.</b>

103
00:06:23.791 --> 00:06:28.958
<b>Understand this in family or social context.</b>

104
00:06:28.958 --> 00:06:33.500
<b>A family member needs your help,</b>

105
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:38.333
<b>and helping them is just a small matter for you.</b>

106
00:06:38.333 --> 00:06:41.958
<b>What a simple situation this is.</b>

107
00:06:41.958 --> 00:06:43.791
<b>But</b>

108
00:06:43.791 --> 00:06:48.125
<b>if expectations dominate your mind,</b>

109
00:06:48.125 --> 00:06:51.291
<b>the mentality changes.</b>

110
00:06:51.291 --> 00:06:55.291
<b>What benefit will you get from helping them?</b>

111
00:06:55.291 --> 00:06:58.083
<b>Or</b>

112
00:06:58.083 --> 00:07:03.458
<b>thinking they didn't help you once before,</b>

113
00:07:03.458 --> 00:07:06.666
<b>so why should you?</b>

114
00:07:06.666 --> 00:07:10.083
<b>How narrow is this thinking.</b>

115
00:07:10.083 --> 00:07:16.125
<b>It distances us from our family and social duties.</b>

116
00:07:16.125 --> 00:07:17.875
<b>Think,</b>

117
00:07:17.875 --> 00:07:21.416
<b>if you were in their place,</b>

118
00:07:21.416 --> 00:07:27.541
<b>and someone refused help for</b>
<b> such petty reasons,</b>

119
00:07:27.541 --> 00:07:30.416
<b>would that be right?</b>

120
00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:37.541
<b>You shouldn't help someone</b>
<b>because you see some benefit in it.</b>

121
00:07:37.541 --> 00:07:44.625
<b>Rather, help because</b>
<b> you are capable of doing so.</b>

122
00:07:49.458 --> 00:07:50.875
<b>Expectations,</b>

123
00:07:50.875 --> 00:07:51.958
<b>profit,</b>

124
00:07:51.958 --> 00:07:52.958
<b>loss,</b>

125
00:07:52.958 --> 00:07:55.833
<b>desires for good or bad outcomes.</b>

126
00:07:55.833 --> 00:08:01.708
<b>And experiencing all this </b>
<b>before work even begins.</b>

127
00:08:01.708 --> 00:08:04.375
<b>How futile is this.</b>

128
00:08:04.375 --> 00:08:09.875
<b>In professional life, countless tasks get </b>
<b>stuck for this very reason,</b>

129
00:08:09.875 --> 00:08:10.916
<b>because</b>

130
00:08:10.916 --> 00:08:23.000
<b>somewhere, someone doesn't fulfill </b>
<b>their duty thinking - what's in it for me?</b>

131
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:30.375
<b>This very greed for benefit</b>
<b> gives birth to corruption.</b>

132
00:08:30.375 --> 00:08:32.375
<b>How wonderful would it be</b>

133
00:08:32.375 --> 00:08:36.583
<b>if everyone fulfilled their duties completely.</b>

134
00:08:36.583 --> 00:08:40.416
<b>All work would flow so smoothly.</b>

135
00:08:40.416 --> 00:08:42.583
<b>Right?</b>

136
00:08:42.583 --> 00:08:47.916
<b>I know you'll surely agree with this point.</b>

137
00:08:47.916 --> 00:08:51.458
<b>Then agree with this too</b>

138
00:08:51.458 --> 00:08:56.750
<b>that the beginning can't come from </b>
<b>anywhere else, it must start with you,</b>

139
00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:59.750
<b>it should start with you.</b>

140
00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:02.291
<b>No one else is in your control.</b>

141
00:09:02.291 --> 00:09:03.625
<b>Only</b>

142
00:09:03.625 --> 00:09:07.750
<b>your work is in your control.</b>

143
00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:11.041
<b>Fulfill your duty completely.</b>

144
00:09:11.041 --> 00:09:14.875
<b>Doing so will bring you immense satisfaction.</b>

145
00:09:14.875 --> 00:09:20.833
<b>You'll also learn to stay away from the </b>
<b>negative effects of emotional ups and downs.</b>

